<%# The product's one-line empty state: "faint grey, one Lucide glyph, one plain
    sentence. Never an illustration, never an emoji."
    (docs/design-system/components/core/EmptyState.jsx + EmptyState.prompt.md.)

    Locals: `message` (REQUIRED); `icon:` a Lucide name, or nil for no glyph
    (default "message-circle"); `tone:` :faint (default) or :muted; `align:` :left
    (default) or :center; `class:` extra utilities.

    `message` is fetched, not defaulted: it is the entire component, so a caller who
    forgets it would otherwise get a faint glyph beside an empty span — a row that
    looks broken but raises nothing. `local_assigns.fetch` makes that a KeyError at the
    call site instead. (Rails strict locals would say this more directly, but `class:`
    is not a legal Ruby parameter name, so the signature is unavailable — see `ui/_card`.)

    `icon: nil` means NO glyph rather than the default one — trending's "Nothing
    trending yet." is a bare sentence, and `lucide_icon(nil)` raises.

    `tone` and `align` are two-valued, so an unrecognised value falls back rather than
    raising: unlike a colour token there is nothing here that can render as a class with
    no rule behind it, and `text-light-grey` vs `text-grey` is a visible difference.

    `p-3` is baked in because four of the five call sites use it. The fifth
    (`hujahs/_response_filter`) wants `px-4 pt-0`; padding utilities of different
    specificity do not reliably override by class order, so that one will need a
    `padding:` local rather than `class:`. Phase 4's call, not this partial's.
%><% message = local_assigns.fetch(:message)
   icon = local_assigns.fetch(:icon, "message-circle")
   tone = (local_assigns[:tone]&.to_sym == :muted) ? "text-grey fill-grey" : "text-light-grey fill-light-grey"
   align = (local_assigns[:align]&.to_sym == :center) ? "justify-center" : "justify-start" %>
<div class="flex items-center gap-1 text-sm p-3 bg-white <%= tone %> <%= align %> <%= local_assigns[:class] %>">
  <%= lucide_icon(icon, class: "w-4 h-4") if icon.present? %>
  <span><%= message %></span>
</div>
